Berdugo, the police are here!

19
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:22,833
Damn!

20
00:01:22,967 --> 00:01:24,233
Block them!

21
00:01:24,367 --> 00:01:28,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

22
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,633
Catch them!

24
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:35,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

25
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:41,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

26
00:01:46,133 --> 00:01:47,700
Open it!

27
00:01:51,567 --> 00:01:55,233
[GUN FIRING]

28
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,067
[GUN FIRING]

29
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:02,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

30
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,000
Shoot them!

31
00:02:05,133 --> 00:02:08,133
[GUN FIRING]

32
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:11,200
[BULLETS PLINKING]

33
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:13,467
[GUN FIRING]

34
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,767
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

35
00:02:17,233 --> 00:02:20,433
[GUN FIRING]

36
00:02:22,567 --> 00:02:23,733
[GUN COCKS]

37
00:02:23,867 --> 00:02:26,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

38
00:02:27,467 --> 00:02:31,533
[GUN FIRING]

39
00:02:31,667 --> 00:02:35,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

40
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:41,633
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

41
00:02:47,833 --> 00:02:49,067
Hold on!

42
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:52,733
[TIRES SCREECH]

43
00:02:52,867 --> 00:02:56,167
[POLICE SIREN WAILING]

44
00:02:56,833 --> 00:02:57,700
What are you doing?

45
00:02:57,833 --> 00:02:59,533
Reverse!

46
00:03:00,267 --> 00:03:02,033
["NEVER SAY DIE"
BY KIM DE LEON PLAYING]

47
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:06,133
Resist them!

48
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:09,200
["NEVER SAY DIE"
BY KIM DE LEON PLAYING]

49
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,800
Lower your gun!

50
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:47,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

51
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:56,867
[GUN CLICKING]

52
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,933
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

53
00:04:03,133 --> 00:04:04,633
Lower your gun!

54
00:04:04,767 --> 00:04:07,967
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

55
00:04:12,067 --> 00:04:14,700
Tomas Limjoco, alias Berdugo,

56
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:16,600
you're under arrest!

57
00:04:17,467 --> 00:04:19,133
- Take him!
- Get down!

58
00:04:19,267 --> 00:04:23,567
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

59
00:04:31,767 --> 00:04:35,733
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:04:37,533 --> 00:04:38,500
You animal!

61
00:04:38,633 --> 00:04:41,867
- [THUDDING]
- [INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

62
00:04:42,767 --> 00:04:44,167
Andrew!

63
00:04:45,233 --> 00:04:47,000
You killed my mother!

64
00:04:47,533 --> 00:04:49,167
- You're an animal!
- Andrew...

65
00:04:50,033 --> 00:04:51,567
Andrew!

66
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,967
This is the end for you,
Berdugo!

67
00:04:56,133 --> 00:04:58,100
You'll rot in prison!

68
00:04:58,233 --> 00:05:01,700
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

69
00:05:15,167 --> 00:05:16,733
Andrew!

70
00:05:16,867 --> 00:05:20,133
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

71
00:05:26,267 --> 00:05:30,367
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:47,033
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

73
00:05:57,467 --> 00:06:01,400
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,633
Matias already confessed.

75
00:06:14,867 --> 00:06:16,533
I know what you're doing.

76
00:06:17,367 --> 00:06:19,467
Good cop, bad cop, right?

77
00:06:21,367 --> 00:06:23,800
Classic interrogation tactic.

78
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:29,133
You separate us,
then tell me he broke.

79
00:06:35,967 --> 00:06:37,333
[BEEPS]

80
00:06:37,467 --> 00:06:40,500
<i>I've been Tomas Limjoco's
right hand for a long time.</i>

81
00:06:41,167 --> 00:06:43,667
<i>He made me pretend
to be Berdugo.</i>

82
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:49,200
<i>But I couldn't refuse because
he held my family as hostage.</i>

83
00:06:50,267 --> 00:06:52,467
<i> I'm begging you.</i>

84
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,967
<i> Make sure my family is safe.</i>

85
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:59,000
<i>I'm ready to testify against him</i>

86
00:06:59,133 --> 00:07:01,333
<i>as long as my wife
and children are safe.</i>

87
00:07:01,467 --> 00:07:05,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

88
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,400
This is the end for you, Tomas.

89
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:11,900
Do you think this is over?

90
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:17,733
Do you think I am
the last syndicate you'd chase?

91
00:07:18,867 --> 00:07:21,467
It doesn't matter to me
how many of you are there.

92
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:26,767
What matters is you're here
in front of me.

93
00:07:28,667 --> 00:07:30,800
There's someone
who wants to talk to you.

94
00:07:30,933 --> 00:07:34,967
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

95
00:07:54,633 --> 00:07:56,567
- [SLAPS]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:59,233
That's for my mother.

97
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,000
[SLAPS]

98
00:08:02,133 --> 00:08:04,333
That's for me.

99
00:08:05,767 --> 00:08:06,600
[SLAPS]

100
00:08:06,733 --> 00:08:09,633
That's for what you did
to my family.

101
00:08:11,267 --> 00:08:14,833
You thought you could control
everything...

102
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:18,567
The people, the truth...

103
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,400
And even us?

104
00:08:20,533 --> 00:08:21,833
You are not God.

105
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,400
You're a demon!

106
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,967
And you know where you'll rot.

107
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:30,567
I'm your husband, Yvette.

108
00:08:32,467 --> 00:08:34,800
I love our children.

109
00:08:34,933 --> 00:08:35,867
We're a family!

110
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,633
Family?
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:41,600
You have no right
to be a husband.

112
00:08:41,733 --> 00:08:44,467
You have no right
to be a father.

113
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:47,667
I'll tell the children
that you're dead.

114
00:08:49,467 --> 00:08:53,633
They will mourn,
but they will move on.

115
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:58,000
I will make sure
they forget you.

116
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,267
They don't deserve
a father like you!

117
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,367
[SLAPS]

118
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:15,467
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:09:23,033 --> 00:09:26,500
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

120
00:09:32,267 --> 00:09:33,500
<i>- Cheers!
- Cheers.</i>

121
00:09:33,633 --> 00:09:35,067
Okay!

122
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,267
So, where's Berdugo?

123
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,033
He's in the provincial jail now.

124
00:09:39,167 --> 00:09:41,667
Good thing Andrew
immediately provided

125
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:44,000
the evidence Ma'am Rebecca kept.

126
00:09:44,133 --> 00:09:46,500
There's no escape
for that Berdugo anymore.

127
00:09:46,633 --> 00:09:48,533
And he has multiple cases
stacked against him.

128
00:09:48,667 --> 00:09:50,133
Many cases.

129
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,333
Why are you smiling?

130
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:02,033
What? What are you saying?

131
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,333
Are you going crazy?

132
00:10:03,467 --> 00:10:04,767
Do you want Liza to haunt you?

133
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:23,833
Cheers!
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:10:23,967 --> 00:10:24,867
- Cheers again.
- Cheers.

135
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,533
Thank you, guys,

136
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:27,733
Thank you, guys.

137
00:10:27,867 --> 00:10:29,167
You look like
you're about to cry.

138
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:30,867
- Are you crying?
- You look so sad!

139
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,600
No, no, hey.
What are you saying?

140
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,200
Wait, I'll join you.

141
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:47,567
What "clingy" are you saying?
You're making false assumptions.

142
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:48,933
Of course, I'll get ready.

143
00:10:49,067 --> 00:10:50,100
I still have to go home
to the province, you know?

144
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:51,967
Right.

145
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:53,800
Oh, before you leave...

146
00:10:53,933 --> 00:10:57,367
Jin Ho, congratulations.

147
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,733
Because you'll be a big help

148
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:00,533
to the intelligence agency
in Korea

149
00:11:00,667 --> 00:11:02,767
if ever that gets formalized.

150
00:11:03,633 --> 00:11:04,733
Congrats.

151
00:11:04,867 --> 00:11:06,033
Thank you.

152
00:11:06,167 --> 00:11:08,333
Guys, this isn't the last time
we'll see each other, okay?

153
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:09,700
Of course!

154
00:11:09,833 --> 00:11:11,267
Of course!

155
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:14,067
So, we'll just update
each other?

156
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:16,700
- See you?
- See you.

157
00:11:16,833 --> 00:11:17,933
- Okay, see you.
- Joey.

158
00:11:18,067 --> 00:11:19,200
See you.

159
00:11:19,333 --> 00:11:20,867
Okay.

160
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:24,933
You're so cute!

161
00:11:25,067 --> 00:11:26,300
[CHUCKLES]

162
00:11:26,433 --> 00:11:27,367
Take care.

163
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:28,867
- Take care.
- Take care, guys.

164
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,133
- Take care.
- Okay.

165
00:11:31,267 --> 00:11:35,467
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

166
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:43,233
If Jin Ho...

167
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,667
is thankful to Berdugo...

168
00:11:48,867 --> 00:11:52,967
As for me, I want to thank you.

169
00:11:53,733 --> 00:11:57,800
For helping us find Berdugo.
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

170
00:11:58,667 --> 00:12:01,433
It wasn't just me.
It was all of us.

171
00:12:01,567 --> 00:12:05,333
I agree, but I also owe you.

172
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:09,800
I want to apologize for...

173
00:12:10,533 --> 00:12:11,933
For everything.

174
00:12:12,067 --> 00:12:16,000
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

175
00:12:16,467 --> 00:12:20,033
For the things I said...

176
00:12:20,567 --> 00:12:21,933
That you're immature,

177
00:12:22,067 --> 00:12:24,100
too young.

178
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:26,100
That wasn't true.

179
00:12:26,233 --> 00:12:32,100
You're strong,
principled, and kind.

180
00:12:32,233 --> 00:12:34,567
You're not hard to love, Joey.

181
00:12:35,133 --> 00:12:39,267
But we both know it's not
the right time, right?

182
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:41,433
I need to focus on my family,

183
00:12:41,567 --> 00:12:43,500
and you need to fix yours.

184
00:12:44,533 --> 00:12:46,300
And...

185
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:48,567
I still have a lot to do.

186
00:12:50,233 --> 00:12:52,033
I need to graduate.

187
00:12:52,167 --> 00:12:53,867
And you still have work.

188
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,500
Talking about work...

189
00:12:56,633 --> 00:12:59,467
I don't even know if I still
have something to go back to,

190
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:01,767
after all that happened.

191
00:13:02,167 --> 00:13:03,733
Why?

192
00:13:03,867 --> 00:13:06,067
You know you have nothing
to fear.

193
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:08,800
I believe you'll get back
on your feet.

194
00:13:08,933 --> 00:13:11,733
And no matter what happens,
I'll still be here.

195
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:14,300
I'll watch you.

196
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,967
To do what?

197
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:20,467
Make reaction videos?

198
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,333
Don't you want that?

199
00:13:26,667 --> 00:13:28,333
I need to go home.

200
00:13:28,467 --> 00:13:32,467
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

201
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:39,233
See you around, Boss Budol.

202
00:13:40,633 --> 00:13:44,233
See you around, Joey On Duty.

203
00:13:52,233 --> 00:13:56,200
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:11,567
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

205
00:14:21,867 --> 00:14:25,233
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

206
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,433
Take care of this, okay?

207
00:14:28,233 --> 00:14:32,500
The next time we meet

208
00:14:32,633 --> 00:14:34,333
and you're still wearing this...

209
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:38,167
it would mean something to me.

210
00:14:41,133 --> 00:14:42,567
We'll see.

211
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:45,933
Okay.

212
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:51,067
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC PLAYING]

213
00:15:06,067 --> 00:15:12,333
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL MUSIC
CONTINUES]

214
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:18,633
By the way, the crawlers
that I had edited earlier...

215
00:15:18,767 --> 00:15:20,267
- is it done?
- Done, Madam.

216
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:21,267
Audio.

217
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:22,767
Andrew...

218
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:24,767
We're about to start.

219
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:26,467
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

220
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:29,433
So? It's your first live
in over a month.

221
00:15:30,633 --> 00:15:32,233
Good luck!

222
00:15:33,533 --> 00:15:34,933
Ready?

223
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,300
We're going live in...

224
00:15:37,433 --> 00:15:42,600
five, four, three, two...

225
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:44,300
<i> Tirada Express!</i>

226
00:15:44,433 --> 00:15:45,667
[GALVANIZING MUSIC PLAYING]

227
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,833
Good day,<i> Tirada</i> viewers.

228
00:15:49,033 --> 00:15:50,600
Did you miss me?

229
00:15:58,867 --> 00:16:00,833
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]
We have so many questions.

230
00:16:00,967 --> 00:16:02,733
But, that's good.

231
00:16:03,467 --> 00:16:05,400
We should be involved.

232
00:16:05,533 --> 00:16:07,033
Some say...

233
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:09,900
I have no obligation to explain.

234
00:16:10,067 --> 00:16:11,567
They have a point.

235
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:15,433
But if you've been watching
for a long time,

236
00:16:15,567 --> 00:16:20,067
you know I don't run away
from questions.

237
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,533
Right?

238
00:16:21,667 --> 00:16:23,167
So, fine.

239
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:25,467
You'll be Boy Abunda today.

240
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:28,600
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

241
00:16:29,967 --> 00:16:33,633
And to those who doubt,
thank you too.

242
00:16:33,767 --> 00:16:38,567
You're important because we're
all searching for the truth.

243
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:42,500
Next time, I'll be more careful,

244
00:16:42,667 --> 00:16:45,400
I'll protect myself more

245
00:16:45,533 --> 00:16:48,967
because it's not just
my name at stake,

246
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:51,500
but your trust.

247
00:16:51,633 --> 00:16:54,367
And as long as there's truth
to reveal,

248
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:56,133
<i> Tirada</i> continues!

249
00:16:56,267 --> 00:16:57,900
More fact checks!

250
00:17:00,567 --> 00:17:01,967
Oh, my god!

251
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,067
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

252
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:05,133
Madam, wow!

253
00:17:05,267 --> 00:17:07,100
178,000 viewers!

254
00:17:07,233 --> 00:17:08,667
- Seriously?
- Yes!

255
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:12,133
Boss!
[WHISPERS]

256
00:17:12,567 --> 00:17:16,400
<i>Saludo viewers, guess
what's happening today!</i>

257
00:17:16,567 --> 00:17:17,833
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:17:17,967 --> 00:17:19,900
<i> Oh, good job guessing!</i>

259
00:17:20,033 --> 00:17:24,700
<i>How did you know
I'm graduating?</i>

260
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:26,400
Yeah!

261
00:17:28,233 --> 00:17:30,400
Wow, I have so many viewers!

262
00:17:30,533 --> 00:17:32,400
Before, there were only
three of you!

263
00:17:32,533 --> 00:17:34,100
Mom! Dad!

264
00:17:34,667 --> 00:17:35,833
Look!

265
00:17:35,967 --> 00:17:37,600
I have 3,000 viewers now!

266
00:17:37,733 --> 00:17:38,800
- Before it was just 3!
- What?

267
00:17:38,933 --> 00:17:40,167
- Let me see!
- Really?

268
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:41,967
Amazing!

269
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:43,300
Even...
[GASPS]

270
00:17:43,433 --> 00:17:45,367
- Yes, there's a lot!
- See, so many!

271
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:46,900
Hello! Hi, everyone!

272
00:17:47,033 --> 00:17:48,600
- 3,000?
- You're right.

273
00:17:48,767 --> 00:17:50,633
Keep supporting Joey, okay?

274
00:17:50,767 --> 00:17:52,000
Thank you, thanks.

275
00:17:52,133 --> 00:17:53,867
Hey, say thank you.

276
00:17:54,333 --> 00:17:55,733
Hello,<i> Saludo</i> viewers!

277
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:57,900
Thank you so much for supporting
my daughter!

278
00:17:58,033 --> 00:17:59,133
Now there are 3,000
of you watching!

279
00:17:59,267 --> 00:18:01,067
Yeah, thank you!

280
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,467
Please share the live.

281
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:04,967
- There!
- Anyway, for today's live...

282
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:07,567
- Let's see.
- I have an announcement...

283
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:09,033
- to them.
- What?

284
00:18:09,167 --> 00:18:11,000
And to you, Mom and Dad.

285
00:18:11,133 --> 00:18:12,400
- What?
- What announcement...

286
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:16,367
Today, I'll reveal...

287
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:17,800
my future career.
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

288
00:18:17,933 --> 00:18:19,667
- Career!
- Career?

289
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,267
My god! Is this it?

290
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:22,667
Career reveal?
There's such a thing?

291
00:18:22,833 --> 00:18:24,233
- No, because...
- Oh, okay.

292
00:18:24,367 --> 00:18:27,167
Many are asking what I'll do
after graduation.

293
00:18:28,867 --> 00:18:30,900
With everything
I've been through,

294
00:18:31,033 --> 00:18:33,300
fighting drugs...

295
00:18:33,433 --> 00:18:37,633
And of course, seeing those
who really dive in to fight.

296
00:18:37,767 --> 00:18:39,067
I was inspired.

297
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:43,833
So, the career I want is...

298
00:18:43,967 --> 00:18:46,800
I want to be...

299
00:18:46,933 --> 00:18:48,733
a police officer!

300
00:18:48,867 --> 00:18:50,200
Police?

301
00:18:50,733 --> 00:18:52,333
- Oh, police? Look...
- Police?

302
00:18:52,467 --> 00:18:54,133
Look at your mother's face, see?

303
00:18:54,267 --> 00:18:55,033
She looks stressed.

304
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,133
Wait, police?

305
00:18:56,267 --> 00:18:57,900
Why?

306
00:18:58,033 --> 00:18:59,467
Joey, maybe...

307
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:03,433
you could consider
to be a pulmonologist?

308
00:19:03,567 --> 00:19:05,233
A principal?

309
00:19:05,367 --> 00:19:06,533
A barangay chief!

310
00:19:06,667 --> 00:19:07,933
Joey, police, really?

311
00:19:08,067 --> 00:19:10,200
So, that's why it's<i> Saludo</i> ,
salute!

312
00:19:10,333 --> 00:19:11,467
She wants to be a policewoman!

313
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:14,233
That's clever, Dad.

314
00:19:14,367 --> 00:19:15,167
If you want to be
a police officer...

315
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:16,500
Fine, I'll support you.

316
00:19:16,633 --> 00:19:18,433
- Let's support her!
- Wait!

317
00:19:18,567 --> 00:19:20,333
Why don't we vote on it?

318
00:19:20,467 --> 00:19:21,967
But that's really what I want,
Mom.

319
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:24,033
Do you want my daughter
to be a policewoman?

320
00:19:24,167 --> 00:19:25,333
Do you want her to be...

321
00:19:25,467 --> 00:19:26,600
They want her
to be a policewoman.

322
00:19:26,733 --> 00:19:28,133
- Police, it's police.
- See?

323
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:29,600
Oh, so many shares.

324
00:19:29,733 --> 00:19:31,133
- You guys...
- So many likes.

325
00:19:31,267 --> 00:19:32,633
Okay, fine.

326
00:19:32,767 --> 00:19:33,700
Police it is!

327
00:19:33,833 --> 00:19:35,533
Go! Support!

328
00:19:35,667 --> 00:19:36,733
If you want to be a police
officer, then police it is.

329
00:19:36,867 --> 00:19:38,533
Oh, you know...

330
00:19:38,667 --> 00:19:40,533
because she'll be
a policewoman...

331
00:19:40,667 --> 00:19:42,333
- Never say die.
- Never say die.

332
00:19:42,467 --> 00:19:45,533
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

333
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:55,133
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:20:03,433 --> 00:20:05,900
<i>Tomas Limjoco,
you're under arrest!</i>

335
00:20:07,867 --> 00:20:09,867
<i>You animal!
[THUDDING]</i>

336
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,067
<i>I'll tell the children
that you're dead.</i>

337
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:16,067
<i> If you think this is the end,</i>

338
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,800
<i> then you're wrong.</i>

339
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,167
<i> I'll come back for you.</i>

340
00:20:21,633 --> 00:20:23,500
You're Berdugo, right?

341
00:20:25,067 --> 00:20:27,100
So, you've been
transferred here?

342
00:20:27,233 --> 00:20:30,000
Nice! Share your goods with me.

343
00:20:30,133 --> 00:20:31,600
I have no supply.

344
00:20:32,133 --> 00:20:33,067
You're so selfish!

345
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,567
Give me some!

346
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:36,067
I said I have none!

347
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:42,000
- [GROANING AND GRUNTING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

348
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:43,867
Get down!

349
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,533
[MAN GROANING]

350
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:48,833
[GROANS]

351
00:20:48,967 --> 00:20:51,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

352
00:20:57,467 --> 00:20:59,200
Where are they?

353
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:03,367
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:13,167
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

355
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:19,400
Andrew...

356
00:21:21,833 --> 00:21:24,133
How are you, Joey On Duty?

357
00:21:24,267 --> 00:21:27,400
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

358
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,000
Wow.

359
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:36,033
The badge.

360
00:21:38,967 --> 00:21:41,100
And the bracelet.

361
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:43,733
Nice combination.

362
00:21:43,867 --> 00:21:45,500
You're still wearing it.

363
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:49,733
Does it mean that...

364
00:21:53,733 --> 00:21:54,767
Joey!

365
00:21:56,133 --> 00:21:57,967
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

366
00:21:58,100 --> 00:21:59,067
Jin Ho!

367
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:00,167
How are you?

368
00:22:02,967 --> 00:22:03,900
Jin Ho!

369
00:22:04,033 --> 00:22:05,133
Andrew.

370
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,400
Just keep it.

371
00:22:08,533 --> 00:22:10,267
We are undercover, remember?

372
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,533
Bro!

373
00:22:12,667 --> 00:22:16,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

374
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:19,600
How are you?

375
00:22:21,667 --> 00:22:22,600
Wait...

376
00:22:22,733 --> 00:22:26,867
I know I'm supposed
to meet Jin Ho and Joey.

377
00:22:27,767 --> 00:22:29,067
Why are you here?

378
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:31,800
Well, I'm not
the only police here.

379
00:22:32,933 --> 00:22:35,567
Do you want me to show you?

380
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:38,167
Oh, look at that!

381
00:22:38,300 --> 00:22:39,267
[CHUCKLES]

382
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,700
Wait, wait.

383
00:22:40,833 --> 00:22:42,100
How did that happen?

384
00:22:42,233 --> 00:22:44,833
This isn't even my jurisdiction,
but...

385
00:22:44,967 --> 00:22:47,967
Well, Jin Ho and Joey missed me.

386
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:49,800
It's okay if you don't.

387
00:22:49,967 --> 00:22:50,967
Andrew misses you.

388
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,800
That's why he teases you.

389
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:56,133
Maybe...

390
00:22:56,267 --> 00:22:57,967
A bit, just a bit.

391
00:22:58,433 --> 00:23:00,433
It's a pleasure.

392
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:02,867
Anyways, how about you?

393
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,867
What's your mission here,
Jin Ho?

394
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,167
Actually, we are looking
for a Korean drug lord.

395
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:10,633
And he has been operating
on an island near here.

396
00:23:10,767 --> 00:23:12,500
Korean drug lord?

397
00:23:12,633 --> 00:23:14,200
- Here?
- Yes.

398
00:23:14,333 --> 00:23:15,833
So, what now?

399
00:23:16,967 --> 00:23:18,100
Let's fight!

400
00:23:18,233 --> 00:23:19,533
Never say die?

401
00:23:21,267 --> 00:23:22,767
Never say die!

402
00:23:22,933 --> 00:23:24,600
Never say die.

403
00:23:25,433 --> 00:23:26,800
Never say die!

404
00:23:26,933 --> 00:23:28,567
- Yes!
- Yes!

405
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:34,567
["NEVER SAY DIE"
BY JILLIAN WARD PLAYING]
